+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` implements the RFC 7396 §2 algorithm (RFC 7386, which it obsoletes, is the same
+algorithm) and returns the merged document as a new value sharing no structure with the inputs; neither is mutated.
+An object patch merges member by member and `null` removes a member; any other patch (including arrays and `null`)
+replaces the target. A non-object target is treated as `{}` when the patch is an object. It never throws. As the RFC
+notes, `null` cannot be set as a member value. `__proto__`, `constructor` and `prototype` are ordinary member names.
