+# Spec: JSON Merge Patch
+
+Request: `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applying a JSON Merge Patch and returning the merged document.
+
+**Standard conflict:** the request cites RFC 7386; that RFC was obsoleted by **RFC 7396** (same algorithm), which the
+constitution names. We implement RFC 7396 §2 (MergePatch pseudocode) exactly.
+
+## Behaviour (RFC 7396 §2)
+- Patch not an object (including array, `null`, scalar): result is a copy of the patch (arrays replaced wholesale).
+- Patch is an object: a non-object target is treated as `{}`; each member with `null` value removes that member;
+  other members are merged recursively. Nulls nested in patch objects that land on a missing target are dropped.
+- Empty-object patch leaves an object target unchanged; on a non-object target it yields `{}`.
+- Neither input is mutated; result shares no structure with inputs. `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` are
+  ordinary member names. Only own members of the target are considered.
+- No errors: every JSON value is a valid patch.
